       The  function  ffiieelldd__iinnffoo returns the sizes and other attributes passed
       in to the field at its creation  time.   The  attributes  are:  height,
       width,  row  of  upper-left corner, column of upper-left corner, number
       off-screen rows, and number of working buffers.

       The function ddyynnaammiicc__ffiieelldd__iinnffoo returns the actual size of  the  field,
       and its maximum possible size.  If the field has no size limit, the lo‐
       cation addressed by the third argument will be set to 0.  A  field  can
       be made dynamic by turning off the OO__SSTTAATTIICC option with ffiieelldd__ooppttss__ooffff.

